WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.870
Let’s look at the feet, and heel pain.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:09.410
Enthesitis means inflammation where a tendon or ligament joins bone.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.030
The Achilles tendon joins the back of the heel.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.150
The plantar fascia attaches at the bottom of the heel.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.280
These are common sore spots in PsA.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.290
A whole toe can also swell up, like a sausage.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:34.100
Tell your team if pain is at the back or bottom of the heel, in a toe, or somewhere else in the foot.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.330
Mention whether walking has become harder.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.620
Heel pain can have several causes.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.800
A picture cannot tell you the cause on its own.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.570
Your team can examine the area, and decide what to check next.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:57.540
Imaging, like X-rays, ultrasound, or MRI, can show changes where tendons attach to bone.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:01.610
Great job! Let’s review.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.700
Heel pain can have several causes.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.430
A symptom picture cannot tell you the cause on its own.
